## Non-Negotiable Reliability Rules

- Never invent venue, citation count, submission target, journal status, or
  author intention.
- If venue is not found in the paper, write `Not found in paper`.
- If a formula, theorem statement, rate, tuning parameter, or constant is not
  reliably extractable, write `needs PDF check`.
- Preserve original theorem, lemma, proposition, corollary, assumption,
  condition, algorithm, and equation numbers.
- Distinguish exact formula, asymptotic limit, upper bound, lower bound,
  consistency, optimality, and oracle optimality.
- Every section must end with `Reliability / Verification status: ...`.

